course: dictionary
lesson: 14394
title: Outcast: someone pushed out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An outcast is a person who is not accepted by other people and is pushed out of a group. You can use outcast as a noun, «She felt like an outcast», or as an adjective, «the outcast kitten sat alone by the bins».
explain: Context shows you the meaning. «The other children would not let Sam join their game, so he sat alone by the fence.» Sam is not allowed in, and he is left on his own. The clues point to outcast meaning someone who is left out.
explain: Stories often ask us to think about outcasts and how they are treated. «Mia was new, and nobody sat with her at lunch.» Many stories ask: what would a kind person do? Including someone is the opposite of making them an outcast.
fact: An outcast is a person who is not accepted and is pushed out of a group or society.
fact: Outcast can be a noun («He was an outcast») or an adjective («outcast children»).
fact: In stories and ethics lessons, outcasts are often characters treated unfairly because they are different.
fact: In the Bible, Jesus spent time with outcasts, such as lepers and tax collectors.
fact: Clue words like «alone», «left out» and «would not let» often show that someone is an outcast.
exercise: «Sam sat alone at lunch, and no one would let him join their game.» What does outcast mean? | Someone who loves lunch | Someone who wins every game | *Someone who is not accepted by others | Someone who is very tall
exercise: «The other children would not let Ben join in, so he stood by the fence.» Which clue shows Ben is an outcast? | He had a new bike | *He was left out and not allowed to join in | He was the fastest runner
exercise: «The old dog was an outcast from the pack.» Find and copy one word that is a noun for a person pushed out. | *outcast | old | dog | pack
test: «Mia was new and different, and nobody talked to her.» What is a clue that Mia is an outcast? | She is tall | *Nobody talks to her or lets her join in | She has a red coat | She likes to read books
test: Which meaning is correct for outcast? | A person in charge of the group | A person who always arrives first | A person who sings very well | *A person who is pushed out of a group
exam: Which action would show kindness to an outcast in a story? | Telling them they cannot sit here | *Asking them to join your game | Laughing at them with your friends | Walking away and never speaking to them
